---
import LessonPage from "../../../components/lesson/LessonPage.astro";
import { defineLesson } from "../../../data/lesson-schema.mjs";
export const page = defineLesson({
  "title": "Possessive adjectives · A0 Grammar",
  "slug": "possessive-adjectives",
  "level": "A0",
  "topic": "Possessive adjectives (my, your, his…)",
  "category": "Grammar",
  "contentType": "grammar",
  "status": "ready",
  "description": "Use my, your, his, her, its, our, and their before a noun to show who owns or is connected to a person or thing.",
  "sequence": 6,
  "prerequisites": [
    "a0/subject-pronouns",
    "a0/this-that-these-those"
  ],
  "related": [
    "a0/regular-plural-nouns",
    "a1/object-pronouns"
  ],
  "assessments": [
    "a0-exit"
  ],
  "tutorReviewRequired": true,
  "qualityReview": {
    "status": "editorial-review",
    "generatedPedagogy": true,
    "learnerPilotCount": 0,
    "scoredItemCount": 37,
    "revisionSummary": "Ownership versus connection, owner reference, singular their, possessive-versus-contraction contrasts, item context, feedback, timing, production, and retrieval were audited; three learner pilots remain."
  }
});
---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="40–45 min" data-extension-duration="10–15 min">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 06</p>
  <h1>Possessive <em>adjectives</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">One small word shows who owns or is connected to a person or thing: <span class="ex">my phone, your manager, her office, their client</span>. Each subject pronoun has a partner, such as <span class="ex">I → my</span>, <span class="ex">she → her</span>, and <span class="ex">they → their</span>. It always sits <strong>before</strong> the noun.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 40–45 min</span>
    <span class="tag">ownership + connection</span>
    <span class="tag">before the noun</span>
    <span class="tag">pronoun → possessive</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Spot the ownership word.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Pair each pronoun with its possessive.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Match, choose, and build chunks.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Describe people, jobs, and things.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">A possessive adjective never changes for one thing or many: <span class="ex">my book / my books</span>, <span class="ex">her client / her clients</span>. The person, group, or thing connected to the noun decides the word, not the noun after it.</p>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Whose side is it connected to?</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">I have a phone. &nbsp;→&nbsp; This is my phone.</span><br /><span class="ex">She has an office. &nbsp;→&nbsp; This is her office.</span><br /><span class="ex">They have a car. &nbsp;→&nbsp; This is their car.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>One word changed in each pair: <strong>I → my</strong>, <strong>she → her</strong>, <strong>they → their</strong>. What connection does the new word show?</li>
      <li>Where does it sit: before the noun, or after it?</li>
      <li>Does the word for "phone, office, car" change? What stays the same?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Each possessive word matches the person, group, or thing connected to the noun that follows it.">
    <h3>Discovery check: read who owns it, then choose</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">The hint in brackets tells you the owner</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="my">my</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="your">your</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="his">his</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="her">her</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="its">its</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="our">our</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="their">their</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>This is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="my" data-hint="The phone belongs to the speaker, so begin with the I → my pair." data-fix="my phone" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> phone. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(it belongs to me)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>That is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="her" data-hint="Elena uses she, so use the she → her pair." data-fix="her office" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> office. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(Elena uses she)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>This is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="his" data-hint="Daniel uses he, so use the he → his pair." data-fix="his desk" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> desk. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(Daniel uses he)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>A new client left a message. I do not know the client’s gender. This is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="their" data-hint="Use the they → their pair when one person’s gender is not known or relevant." data-fix="their message" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> message.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>You have a coffee. This is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="your" data-hint="I am speaking to you, so use the you → your pair." data-fix="your coffee" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> coffee.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The company has a new logo. This is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="its" data-hint="The logo belongs to one company, so use the it → its pair." data-fix="its logo" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> logo.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: one partner for each pronoun</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Every subject pronoun has one possessive partner. Learn them as pairs:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>subject pronoun</th><th>possessive adjective</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>I</b></td><td><b>my</b></td><td><span class="contraction">my phone</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>you</b></td><td><b>your</b></td><td><span class="contraction">your email</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>he</b></td><td><b>his</b></td><td><span class="contraction">his client</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>she</b></td><td><b>her</b></td><td><span class="contraction">her office</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>it</b></td><td><b>its</b></td><td><span class="contraction">its name</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>we</b></td><td><b>our</b></td><td><span class="contraction">our team</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>they</b></td><td><b>their</b></td><td><span class="contraction">their car · their name</span> (many people or one person)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Does the possessive go before or after the noun? <strong>Before:</strong> <span class="ex">my manager</span>, never <span class="ex">manager my</span>.</li>
      <li>Is it <span class="ex">his</span> or <span class="ex">her</span>? Look at the person connected to the noun, not the noun itself. Daniel uses he, so say <span class="ex">his office</span>. Elena uses she, so say <span class="ex">her car</span>.</li>
      <li>Does the word change for one or many? <strong>No.</strong> <span class="ex">my book</span> and <span class="ex">my books</span> both use <em>my</em>.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">Their</span> can connect one person or many people to a noun: <span class="ex">My parents sold their car.</span> <span class="ex">Someone left their phone.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Possessive word or contraction?</h3>
    <p>The possessive word sits before a noun. The contraction contains the verb <span class="ex">are</span> or <span class="ex">is</span>.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>before a noun</th><th>subject + verb</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><span class="ex">your phone</span></td><td><span class="ex">you’re early</span> = you are early</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="ex">its name</span></td><td><span class="ex">it’s new</span> = it is new</td></tr>
        <tr><td><span class="ex">their office</span></td><td><span class="ex">they’re upstairs</span> = they are upstairs</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>In ordinary speech, each pair can sound the same. Use the sentence job to choose the written form: noun next means <span class="ex">your, its, their</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="thinking-card" data-lesson-extension="Optional same-sound listening check">
    <h3>Same sound, different sentence job</h3>
    <p>Look away from the script. Your tutor reads each pair. Say “possessive” when a noun follows and “subject plus verb” when the phrase contains <span class="ex">are</span> or <span class="ex">is</span>.</p>
    <details>
      <summary>Tutor script and answers</summary>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="ex">Your phone is here.</span> (possessive) · <span class="ex">You’re early.</span> (you are)</li>
        <li><span class="ex">Its name is Luna.</span> (possessive) · <span class="ex">It’s new.</span> (it is)</li>
        <li><span class="ex">Their office is upstairs.</span> (possessive) · <span class="ex">They’re upstairs.</span> (they are)</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
  </div>

  <h2>From pronoun to possessive</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Keep the pairs together. Say each one aloud: <span class="ex">I → my, you → your, he → his, she → her, it → its, we → our, they → their.</span></p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Sound natural: keep the owner word with its noun</h3>
    <p>A possessive adjective and its noun make one chunk. In a neutral sentence, the noun usually carries the strongest beat.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>chunk</th><th>natural rhythm</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>my phone</td><td>my <b>PHONE</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>her office</td><td>her <b>OFF</b>ice</td></tr>
        <tr><td>our team</td><td>our <b>TEAM</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>their car</td><td>their <b>CAR</b></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Do not pause between the two words. Make the owner word strong only when you correct ownership: <span class="ex">It’s <strong>MY</strong> phone, not your phone.</span> In ordinary American speech, <span class="ex">your</span> and <span class="ex">their</span> are usually quick one-syllable words.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game data-lesson-extension="Optional pronoun-pair matching" data-success-message="Correct. You matched I, you, he, she, it, we, and they with my, your, his, her, its, our, and their.">
    <h3>Drill 1: match each pronoun to its possessive</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap a possessive word, then tap the pronoun it belongs to</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="i">my</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="you">your</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="he">his</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="she">her</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="it">its</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="we">our</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="they">their</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="i" data-hint="The speaker says I." data-fix="I → my" data-placeholder="I">I</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="you" data-hint="The speaker says you to the listener." data-fix="you → your" data-placeholder="you">you</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="he" data-hint="Use this subject with his." data-fix="he → his" data-placeholder="he">he</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="she" data-hint="Use this subject with her." data-fix="she → her" data-placeholder="she">she</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="it" data-hint="Use this subject with its." data-fix="it → its" data-placeholder="it">it</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="we" data-hint="This subject includes the speaker and other people." data-fix="we → our" data-placeholder="we">we</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="they" data-hint="This subject can mean other people or one person whose gender is not stated." data-fix="they → their" data-placeholder="they">they</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. His follows a person who uses he, and her follows a person who uses she; the noun does not decide the word.">
    <h3>Drill 2: his or her? Look at the owner</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">The name in brackets tells you who owns it</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="his">his</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="her">her</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Daniel is reading <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="his" data-hint="Daniel uses he, so use the he → his pair." data-fix="his email" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> email. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(Daniel uses he)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Elena is in <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="her" data-hint="Elena uses she, so use the she → her pair." data-fix="her office" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> office. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(Elena uses she)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Mr. Lopez is with <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="his" data-hint="Mr. Lopez uses he, so use his before client." data-fix="his client" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> client. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(Mr. Lopez uses he)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>My manager Sofia is on <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="her" data-hint="Sofia uses she, so use her before phone." data-fix="her phone" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> phone. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(Sofia uses she)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The new coworker Marco lost <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="his" data-hint="Marco uses he, so use his before keys, even though keys is plural." data-fix="his keys" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> keys. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(Marco uses he)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="this is her laptop" data-hint="Begin with This is, then place the possessive before laptop." data-fix="This is her laptop." data-success-message="Correct. Her comes directly before laptop because Elena uses she and the laptop is connected to her.">
    <h3>Drill 3: build the sentence</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The laptop belongs to Elena. Build the sentence, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="laptop">laptop</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="this">This</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="her">her</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="their office is upstairs" data-hint="Begin with the sales team’s possessive word, then add office is upstairs." data-fix="Their office is upstairs." data-success-message="Correct. Their comes before office because the office belongs to the sales team, a they group.">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the sentence</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The office belongs to the sales team. Build the sentence.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="office">office</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="their">Their</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="upstairs">upstairs</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="he" data-hint="Phone needs a word before it that shows its connection to Daniel." data-fix="His phone is new." data-why="Before a noun we use the possessive his, not the subject pronoun he.">
    <h3>Drill 5: pronoun or possessive?</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. The phone belongs to Daniel.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="he">He</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="phone">phone</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="new">new.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="we" data-hint="Car needs the possessive partner of we before it." data-fix="Our car is fast." data-why="Before a noun we use the possessive our, not the subject pronoun we.">
    <h3>Drill 6: pronoun or possessive?</h3>
    <p>You are speaking about the car that belongs to you and your family. Tap the wrong word.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="we">We</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="car">car</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="fast">fast.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="it's" data-hint="A noun comes next, so the sentence needs a possessive word, not it is." data-fix="The app changed its name." data-why="Its shows the app’s connection to the name. It’s means it is.">
    <h3>Drill 7: its or it’s?</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="app">app</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="changed">changed</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="it's">it’s</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="name">name.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform data-lesson-extension="Optional no-choice pronoun transformation">
    <h3>Drill 8: change the pronoun, then say it</h3>
    <p>Say the possessive aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> he &nbsp;→&nbsp; ___ client</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>his</strong> client</p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> they &nbsp;→&nbsp; ___ office</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>their</strong> office</p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> she &nbsp;→&nbsp; ___ manager</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>her</strong> manager</p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> we &nbsp;→&nbsp; ___ team</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>our</strong> team</p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> I &nbsp;→&nbsp; ___ coworkers</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>my</strong> coworkers</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your desk:</b> Name four things at your desk with <span class="ex">my</span>. <span class="ex">This is my phone. These are my notes. That is my coffee.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your team:</b> Tell me about three coworkers. Use <span class="ex">his</span>, <span class="ex">her</span>, or <span class="ex">their</span> for their jobs, relationships, and things. <span class="ex">Daniel is on a call with his client. Elena is in her office. Alex uses they and is with their manager.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your family:</b> Describe two family members and what they own. <span class="ex">My sister is a nurse. Her car is small. My parents have a dog. Their dog is friendly.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Our place:</b> Describe your workplace or home with <span class="ex">our</span>. <span class="ex">This is our office. Our team is small. Our meeting room is upstairs.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Whose is it? (info gap):</b> Your teacher names a person and an object. Answer with the possessive: <span class="ex">Daniel, keys. → These are his keys.</span> Continue with new people and things.</div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Success check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Use at least four different possessive words before nouns.</li>
      <li>Choose from the person, group, or thing connected to the noun.</li>
      <li>Use <span class="ex">their</span> for one person when gender is not known or relevant.</li>
      <li>Keep <span class="ex">its</span> separate from <span class="ex">it’s = it is</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the pairs</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “<strong>I → ___</strong>, <strong>you → ___</strong>, <strong>he → ___</strong>, <strong>she → ___</strong>, <strong>we → ___</strong>, <strong>they → ___</strong>.”</p>
    <p>Then say one true sentence about something <strong>you</strong> own and one about something <strong>a coworker or family member</strong> owns, using <em>his</em>, <em>her</em>, or <em>their</em>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Excellent. You matched each reference with its possessive word, placed it before the noun, and separated its from it’s.">
    <h3>Final quiz: choose the owner word</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="my" data-hint="The phone belongs to the speaker, so use the I → my pair." data-fix="my phone">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. (it belongs to me) This is ___ phone.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="my">my</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="your">your</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="his">his</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="her" data-hint="Elena uses she, so choose the she → her pair." data-fix="her office">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. (Elena = she) She is in ___ office.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="his">his</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="her">her</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="their">their</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="his" data-hint="Daniel uses he, so choose the he → his pair." data-fix="his email">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. (Daniel = he) Daniel is reading ___ email.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="her">her</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="his">his</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="its">its</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="their" data-hint="The sales team is a they group." data-fix="their meeting room">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. (the sales team = they) This is ___ meeting room.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="our">our</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="your">your</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="their">their</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="our" data-hint="The speaker is inside the team, so the group includes we." data-fix="Our team is small.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. You are speaking as a member of the team. ___ team is small.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="our">our</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="their">their</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="my">my</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="His office is upstairs." data-hint="Marco uses he. The possessive must come before office." data-fix="His office is upstairs.">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. Which sentence is correct? (the office belongs to Marco, who uses he)</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="His office is upstairs.">His office is upstairs.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="He office is upstairs.">He office is upstairs.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Office his is upstairs.">Office his is upstairs.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="my books" data-hint="The speaker still uses my when more than one book follows." data-fix="my books">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. I have more than one book. Which is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="my books">my books</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="mine books">mine books</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="my book's">my book's</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="your" data-hint="I am speaking directly to you, so use the you → your pair." data-fix="your coffee">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. (I am talking to you) Is this ___ coffee?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="my">my</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="your">your</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="their">their</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="their" data-hint="The caller is one person, but the person’s gender is not known." data-fix="their message">
        <p class="quiz-question">9. A delivery driver called, but you do not know the driver’s gender. This is ___ message.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="his">his</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="its">its</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="their">their</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="its" data-hint="A noun comes after the gap, so use the company’s possessive word, not it is." data-fix="its name">
        <p class="quiz-question">10. The company changed ___ name after the merger.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="it">it</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="it’s">it’s</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="its">its</button></div>
